      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining OAuth Callback**\n\nI'm starting to formalize the plan to build `oauth_callback.py`. I've settled on Google's OAuth 2.0 API as the external provider to make the implementation more concrete. This choice allows me to move beyond general concepts and start mapping out the specific steps for authorization code exchange.\n\n\n**Mapping Callback Implementation**\n\nI've fleshed out the initial structure for `oauth_callback.py`, focusing on handling the OAuth callback with Google. A Flask route will manage the incoming requests, and I'll use `requests` for the token exchange. Specific Google identifiers, such as endpoint URLs, client ID, and secret, are now included in the preliminary plan.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789867344986,
          "start": 1789867342814
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc683bde001HqtKMs0j7UJtIw",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc6837c1001EfoczDYzhSDzR7",
